## 🛠️ Setting Up Your Dev Environment (The Detailed Way)

### Full Stack Setup (Do This First Time)

#### Part 1: Get the Code
```bash
git clone https://github.com/tuwana/jpe-sims4.git
cd jpe-sims4
```

#### Part 2: Python Setup
```bash
# Make a separate Python environment (trust me, do this)
python -m venv venv

# Activate it
source venv/bin/activate  # Mac/Linux
# OR
venv\Scripts\activate  # Windows

# Install everything for development
pip install -e ".[dev]"

# Verify it worked
python -c "import jpe_sims4; print('Python side is good!')"
python -m pytest tests/ --collect-only
```

#### Part 3: JavaScript Setup
```bash
# Get all the Node packages
npm install

# Make sure the code is clean
npm run lint
npm run type-check
```

#### Part 4: Verify Everything
```bash
# Run tests for both sides
npm run test:all

# Or do them separate
npm test          # Frontend tests
python -m pytest  # Backend tests
```

### IDE Setup (Pick Your Weapon)

**If You Use VSCode (Recommended for full stack):**
Install these extensions:
- Python (by Microsoft) - for Python development
- Pylance - for smart Python help
- TypeScript Vue Plugin - for React/TypeScript
- Tailwind CSS IntelliSense - for styling
- Prettier - for code formatting

**If You Use PyCharm (Best for backend work):**
- Built-in Python support
- Built-in Node.js/TypeScript support
- Excellent debugging tools
- No extra setup needed, just open the folder

