## 🧪 Testing (Making Sure Everything Works)

### Frontend Tests (React)

```bash
npm test                # Run all frontend tests
npm test:watch          # Auto-run as you code
npm test:coverage       # See coverage report

# Test specific file
npm test -- Button.test.tsx

# Test matching pattern
npm test -- --grep "button"
```

Here's a test example:

```typescript
import { render, screen } from '@testing-library/react'
import Button from '@/components/common/Button'

describe('Button Component', () => {
  it('renders with correct text', () => {
    render(<Button>Click me</Button>)
    expect(screen.getByRole('button')).toHaveTextContent('Click me')
  })

  it('calls onClick when clicked', () => {
    const handleClick = jest.fn()
    render(<Button onClick={handleClick}>Click</Button>)

    screen.getByRole('button').click()
    expect(handleClick).toHaveBeenCalled()
  })
})
```

### Backend Tests (Python)

```bash
python -m pytest tests/                    # All tests
python -m pytest tests/test_engine.py -v   # One file, detailed
python -m pytest -k "validator" -v         # Tests with "validator" in name
python -m pytest --cov=jpe_sims4           # With coverage
```

Here's a test example:

```python
def test_engine_parses_jpe():
    """Make sure the engine can read JPE files"""
    engine = Engine()
    ir = engine.parse_jpe_file("tests/fixtures/simple.jpe")

    assert ir is not None
    assert isinstance(ir, ProjectIR)

def test_validator_catches_errors():
    """Make sure validation works"""
    validator = Validator()

    # Bad interaction (missing required stuff)
    bad_interaction = Interaction(name="test")
    errors = validator.validate_interaction(bad_interaction)

    # Should have caught the error
    assert len(errors) > 0
```

### End-to-End Tests (Real Browser)

These actually run the full app and test it like a user would:

```bash
npm run test:e2e                # Run all E2E tests
npm run test:e2e:ui             # With visual interface
npm run test:e2e:debug          # Debug mode
npm run test:e2e:report         # View report after running
```

### Running Everything

```bash
npm run test:all    # Runs both frontend and backend tests
```

