## 📚 Git Workflow (Keep Things Clean)

### Branch Names

```
feature/description       # New features
fix/description          # Bug fixes
chore/description        # Maintenance
docs/description         # Documentation
refactor/description     # Code cleanup
```

### Commit Messages

```
feat: Add button component with variants
fix: Resolve editor lag on large files
chore: Update dependencies
docs: Add deployment guide
test: Add validation tests
```

### The Process

```bash
# 1. Create your branch
git checkout -b feature/my-feature

# 2. Make changes and commit
git add .
git commit -m "feat: Add my feature"

# 3. Push to remote
git push -u origin feature/my-feature

# 4. Create pull request (on GitHub)
# Wait for review and CI/CD checks

# 5. Merge and update local
git checkout main
git pull origin main
git rebase origin/main feature/my-feature
```

---

## 🎨 Design System Rules (Keep Everything Consistent)

### Rule 1: Use Design Tokens (No Hardcoding Colors)

```tsx
// ✅ Right
<div className="bg-background-secondary text-text-primary p-4 rounded-lg">
  <h2 className="text-xl font-semibold">Heading</h2>
  <p className="text-text-secondary">Description</p>
</div>

// ❌ Wrong
<div style={{ backgroundColor: '#1E2633', padding: '16px' }}>
  This is bad!
</div>
```

### Rule 2: Component Locations

```
src/components/
├── common/          # Atomic components (Button, Input, Modal)
├── layout/          # Layout pieces (Sidebar, EditorPane, TitleBar)
├── modals/          # Dialog boxes
├── editor/          # Editor-specific
└── [features]/      # Feature-specific stuff
```

### Rule 3: Use Tailwind (Utility-First)

```tsx
// ✅ Right - Tailwind with design tokens
<div className="bg-background-secondary p-4 border border-border-subtle rounded-lg">
  {children}
</div>

// ❌ Wrong - Inline styles
<div style={{ backgroundColor: '#1E2633', padding: '16px' }}>
  Bad!
</div>
```

### Rule 4: Responsive Design

```tsx
// Works on all screen sizes
<div className="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-4">
  {items.map(item => <Card key={item.id}>{item}</Card>)}
</div>
```

### Rule 5: Accessibility

```tsx
// ✅ Right - Accessible
<button
  aria-label="Close dialog"
  className="p-2 hover:bg-background-tertiary rounded focus:outline-none focus:ring-2 focus:ring-accent-primary"
>
  ✕
</button>

// ❌ Wrong - Not accessible
<div onClick={handleClose}>X</div>
```

### Rule 6: Component Composition

Every component needs:
- Props interface
- `className` prop support
- TypeScript types
- Sensible defaults

```tsx
interface CardProps extends React.HTMLAttributes<HTMLDivElement> {
  variant?: 'default' | 'elevated'
}

export default function Card({
  variant = 'default',
  className = '',
  children,
  ...props
}: CardProps) {
  return (
    <div
      className={`bg-background-secondary p-4 rounded-lg ${
        variant === 'elevated' && 'shadow-lg'
      } ${className}`}
      {...props}
    >
      {children}
    </div>
  )
}
```

### Rule 7: State Management

```typescript
// App-wide state → Zustand
export const useProjectStore = create(...)

// Component-local state → React hooks
const [isOpen, setIsOpen] = useState(false)
```

### Rule 8: Memoization (Keep It Fast)

```tsx
// For expensive components
const FileItem = React.memo(({ file }) => {
  return <div>{file.name}</div>
})

// For computed values
const expensive = useMemo(() => {
  return computeSomethingHeavy(data)
}, [data])

// For callback functions
const handleClick = useCallback(() => {
  doSomething()
}, [])
```

### Rule 9: Import Organization

```tsx
// 1. React stuff
import { useState } from 'react'

// 2. Third-party
import { useProjectStore } from '@/stores/useProjectStore'

// 3. Internal stuff
import Button from '@/components/common/Button'

// 4. Types
import type { Project } from '@/types'
```

### Rule 10: Spacing Uses 4px Base

- `p-1` = 4px
- `p-2` = 8px
- `p-4` = 16px (most common)
- `p-6` = 24px
- `p-8` = 32px

